# Code Quality Standards

## General Standards

- No unused imports or variables (enforced by strict TypeScript config)
- Consistent error handling with proper context
- Type safety throughout codebase
- Clean, focused functions with single responsibility
- Use `Set`/`Map` for deduplication when needed
- Handle edge cases (null checks, empty arrays, etc.)

## Error Handling Pattern

```typescript
try {
	// operation code
} catch (error) {
	console.error('Failed to fetch collections', error);
	throw new NodeApiError(this.getNode(), error, { itemIndex: index });
}
```

## Data Validation

- Check for missing required parameters
- Validate API responses before processing
- Handle undefined/null values safely
- Use type guards for type narrowing

## Loop & Recursion

- Use clear variable names in loops (e.g., `index`, `entry`)
- Document recursive functions
- Prevent infinite loops with base cases
- Use functional approaches (map, filter) when appropriate

## Performance

- Avoid N+1 queries
- Cache repeated computations
- Use early returns to reduce nesting
- Keep functions focused and under 150 lines

## Testing

- All changes should pass linting: `pnpm lint`
- Build should succeed: `pnpm build`
- Watch mode for development: `pnpm build:watch`
